Well, there's actually quite a bit of disagreement in here about how 
useful gaining levels beyond level 14 is. One school of thought states 
that it actually makes the game harder, since higher level monsters will 
tend to spawn more often, and since the extra hit- and manapoints can be 
gotten easily through other means it's just not worth the risk.
Some disagree with this, arguing that the monster-generation isn't all 
that affected by your level, not enough, at least, that forgoing the 
extra level benifits is sensible.

I personally think you're plenty prepared for ascension, provided you 
remember take the necessary care. Maximize enchantments on your armour, 
if you haven't already, and head on up. Or down. Whichever.
Oh, and a bit of alchemy wouldn't hurt, if you've found out how to do 
that. If you haven't, and don't mind using spoilers, a quick use of the 
Google search engine should help you lots.


